  "body": "### What is the issue with the HTML Standard?\n\n```data:text/html,<select style=\"width: 40px\"><option>Something probably longer</option>```\r\n\r\nInteroperably clips the contents regardless of appearance, but this is to the best of my knowledge not specified anywhere. Firefox does this via `overflow: clip` in an internal anonymous box but also has `overflow: clip` on the `<select>` itself.\r\n\r\nWebKit and Blink probably do the same (clipping internally?).\r\n\r\nI propose to do something like we did for buttons and make non-listbox select have `overflow: clip !important` in the UA sheet rather than magic.\r\n\r\nSimilarly, listbox selects have scrollable overflow on Firefox by default, but `overflow: visible` in WebKit and Blink, yet they are scrollable. @mfreed7 @nt1m do you know how WebKit / Blink make listbox scrollable?\r\n\r\nThanks.",
